Requirements: 29   with obligations: 28   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] The completion verdict accounts for every requirement of the mandate, so a
    review cannot report that it found no material gaps while part of the mandate
    produced nothing it was able to judge.
    -> completion-verdict-covers-all-requirements  [functional/explicit]
       The completion verdict accounts for every requirement of the mandate, so no part
       of the mandate can produce nothing it is able to judge while the review reports
       no material gaps.

[constraint-01] A requirement deliberately declined with a stated reason does not count
    against how much of the mandate the review covered.
    -> declined-requirement-coverage-accounting  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-02)
       A requirement deliberately declined with a stated reason does not count against
       how much of the mandate the review covered.

[constraint-02] An open question that the change itself answers yields an obligation
    stating the behaviour the change committed to.
    -> answered-open-question-yields-obligation  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-03)
       An open question answered by the change yields an obligation stating the
       behaviour the change committed to.

[constraint-03] An obligation derived from an answered open question cites the places in
    the change that answer it, and is treated as implemented on the strength of those
    citations rather than being reported as missing.
    -> answered-open-question-implemented-with-citations  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-04)
       An obligation derived from an answered open question is treated as implemented
       and cites the places in the change that answer it.

[constraint-04] An obligation derived from an answered open question is carried on the
    test evidence axis like any other, so a settled implementation choice that no test
    exercises prevents a report of no material gaps.
    -> answered-open-question-untested-blocks-no-gaps  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-05)
       An obligation derived from an answered open question that no test exercises
       prevents a report of no material gaps.

[constraint-05] An open question the change does not answer yields no obligation.
    -> constraint-05-unanswered-open-question-yields-no-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       An open question the change does not answer yields no obligation.

[constraint-06] Task-file text that yielded no requirement at all prevents a report of
    no material gaps.
    -> no-requirement-text-blocks-no-gaps  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-07)
       Task-file text that yielded no requirement at all prevents a report of no
       material gaps.

[constraint-07] How much of the mandate the review covered is recorded on the completion
    result and stated in the report.
    -> record-coverage-on-result-and-report  [functional/explicit]
       Record how much of the mandate the review covered on the completion result and
       state it in the report.

[constraint-08] Covering less than the whole mandate only ever bounds the verdict and
    never raises it, so a review that covers less of the mandate never reports a better
    result than the same review covering more of it.
    -> coverage-only-bounds-verdict  [invariant/explicit]
       Treat reduced mandate coverage as a one-way bound on the verdict so that covering
       less of the mandate never improves the reported result.

[constraint-09] The completion verdict is derived from the review's own recorded state
    without consulting a model.
    -> verdict-from-recorded-state-no-model  [functional/explicit]
       Derive the completion verdict from the review's recorded state without consulting
       a model.

[constraint-10] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> byte-identical-inputs-byte-identical-review-state  [invariant/explicit]
       Produce byte-identical review state for two runs over byte-identical task text.

[constraint-11] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> tests-issue-no-live-model-calls  [compatibility/explicit]
       Keep tests free of live model calls.

[exclusion-01] Whether a requirement that was deliberately declined was correctly
    declined; the stated reason is taken at face value and not re-judged.
    -> decline-reason-not-rejudged  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the stated reason for a deliberately declined requirement as accepted at
       face value when assessing coverage.

[exclusion-02] How an obligation's test evidence is rated once it reaches the rating
    stage, which is #180.
    -> exclude-test-evidence-rating-stage  [invariant/explicit]
       Leave the rating stage for an obligation's test evidence outside this change's
       scope.

[exclusion-03] How stable decomposition is from one run to the next, which is #193.
    -> exclude-stable-decomposition-across-runs  [invariant/explicit]
       Leave decomposition stability from one run to the next outside this change's
       scope.

[exclusion-04] Measuring how accurate decomposition is, which is #211.
    -> exclude-decomposition-accuracy  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not measure how accurate decomposition is.

[exclusion-05] How finely a single requirement is split into obligations, which is #117.
    -> exclude-split-granularity  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter how finely a single requirement is split into
       obligations.

[exclusion-06] Whether obligation identifiers are stable across task-file edits, which
    is #231.
    -> exclude-obligation-id-stability-across-edits  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not address whether obligation identifiers are stable across
       task-file edits.

[exclusion-07] Which tests are discovered, and which obligations they are mapped to.
    -> exclude-test-discovery-and-mapping  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not determine which tests are discovered or which obligations
       they are mapped to.

